several different authors. No third-party SOURCE CODE is present — only test
fixtures (tiny standalone XML documents whose only content is markup, plus a
one-line English description each).

## W3C XML Conformance Test Suite (xmlconf) — a license-filtered slice

The vendored fixtures reproduce a subset of the official W3C XML Conformance
Test Suite, release `xmlts20080827.zip`
(https://www.w3.org/XML/Test/xmlts20080827.zip, published 2008-08-27, the
release current as of this vendoring), whose overall manifest is
`xmlconf/xmlconf.xml`. That manifest aggregates SEVERAL independently
copyrighted sub-suites contributed by different organizations over the life
of the XML Core Working Group's conformance effort; their terms are NOT
uniform, so each is accounted for separately below rather than treated as one
blanket grant.

  * vendored verbatim under `src/testdata/xmlconf/` (130 fixture files,
    grouped by originating sub-suite: `sun-valid/`, `sun-not-wf/`,
    `ibm-valid/`, `ibm-not-wf/`, `eduni-ns10/`)
  * driven mechanically by `src/xmlconf_vectors.zig` (one entry per file,
    `@embedFile`d, tagged `reject`/`accept` by the manifest's own TYPE) and
    `src/xmlconf_test.zig` (the runner)

